+# TASK-260923-3e4i3n — native-policy-conflict-refusal results
+
+## Implementation
+
+Decision 0018 item 4 is enforced in Claude and Codex yolo scans through the existing `nativeargs.FlagIndexes` / `SplitFlagValue` grammar. Native mode performs no argv inspection and forwards the caller's arguments verbatim. Codex scans both top-level and `exec` placements. Known non-conflicting selectors remain forwarded.
+
+The expanded closed selector grammar is `permission-grammar-v2`; the Claude and Codex capability rows name v2, while Pi retains v1. This token change records the larger refusal grammar. The binary version is injected by the Makefile from `git describe`; there is no separate module version constant to change. The next free release is v0.5.20 because the current HEAD is tagged v0.5.19. The changelog names v0.5.20; tag creation remains the orchestrator's post-landing step.
+
+Exported errors for launcher mapping:
+
+- `agentic.ErrNativePolicyConflict` — stable `errors.Is` classification for known conflicts.
+- `*agentic.NativePolicyConflictError` — `errors.As` details through `Selector` and `Placement`.
+- `agentic.NativePolicyPlacementFlag`, `...Equals`, `...SeparateToken`, and `...AttachedShort` — stable placement values.
+- `agentic.ErrPermissionModeDuplicate` — existing stable sentinel for the module-mapped bypass flag appearing again in native args.
+- `agentic.ErrNativePolicyUnknown` — malformed selectors and unknown or invalid values remain fail-closed.
+
+## Executed selector matrix
+
+Each matrix row drove `BuildPlan` in yolo and native modes. Yolo refused; the native twin built and preserved the selector in argv. Codex rows ran at top level and after `exec`.
+
+| Provider / selector family | Forms and placements | Yolo rows | Native rows |
+|---|---|---:|---:|
+| Claude `--permission-mode` | Six values (`acceptEdits`, `auto`, `bypassPermissions`, `manual`, `dontAsk`, `plan`) × separate-token and `=` | 12 conflict | 12 forwarded |
+| Claude `--allow-dangerously-skip-permissions` | Bare and `=true` | 2 conflict | 2 forwarded |
+| Claude `--restricted` | Bare and `=true` | 2 conflict | 2 forwarded |
+| Claude mapped bypass duplicate | `--dangerously-skip-permissions`, bare and `=true` | 2 `ErrPermissionModeDuplicate` | 2 forwarded |
+| **Claude total** | 18 selector/form rows per mode | **18** | **18** |
+| Codex `-a` / `--ask-for-approval` | Two spellings × separate-token and `=` × top-level and `exec` | 8 conflict | 8 forwarded |
+| Codex `-s` / `--sandbox` | Two spellings × separate-token and `=` × top-level and `exec` | 8 conflict | 8 forwarded |
+| Codex `--approve-for-me` | Bare and `=true` × top-level and `exec` | 4 conflict | 4 forwarded |
+| Codex `--dangerously-bypass-*` family | `--dangerously-bypass-hook-trust` bare/`=` plus a second wildcard-prefix selector, each at top-level and `exec` | 6 conflict | 6 forwarded |
+| Codex mapped bypass duplicate | `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox`, bare and `=` × top-level and `exec` | 4 `ErrPermissionModeDuplicate` | 4 forwarded |
+| Codex policy config keys | Three keys × five encodings (`-c` separate/`=`, `--config` separate/`=`, attached `-c`) × top-level and `exec` | 30 conflict | 30 forwarded |
+| **Codex total** | 30 selector/form rows × top-level and `exec`, per mode | **60** | **60** |
+| **Combined total** | One executed subtest per selector/form/mode (including Codex command placement) | **78** | **78** |
+
+Additional tests forward Claude `--debug`, `--verbose`, and `-d`, plus Codex `model_reasoning_effort`, `service_tier`, `mcp_servers.*`, and `--search` under yolo. Six malformed or invalid Codex `-a` / `-s` cases fail with `ErrNativePolicyUnknown`. Native tests with unknown selectors and an unestablished release also preserve the raw argv.
+
+## Narrowing mutants
+
+Mutants ran in a disposable `.mutation-copy` module copy inside this Story worktree; they did not alter candidate source files. Each targeted `go test` command below exited 1 because the corresponding matrix assertion failed, so the mutant was killed. The Codex mapped-bypass mutant was also caught: its `=true` form still refused through the wildcard branch but lost the required `ErrPermissionModeDuplicate` classification, which the matrix asserts.
+
+| Refusal family narrowed | Targeted command | Exit | Result |
+|---|---|---:|---|
+| Claude known permission-mode values | `go test ./pkg/agentic/systems/claude -run '^TestPermissionModeConflictMatrix$'` | 1 | Killed; yolo rows admitted |
+| Claude `--allow-dangerously-skip-permissions` | `go test ./pkg/agentic/systems/claude -run '^TestOtherKnownClaudePolicyConflicts$'` | 1 | Killed; yolo rows admitted |
+| Claude `--restricted` | `go test ./pkg/agentic/systems/claude -run '^TestOtherKnownClaudePolicyConflicts$'` | 1 | Killed; yolo rows admitted |
+| Claude mapped-bypass duplicate form | `go test ./pkg/agentic/systems/claude -run '^TestOtherKnownClaudePolicyConflicts$'` | 1 | Killed; equals form admitted |
+| Codex `-a` / `--ask-for-approval` aliases | `go test ./pkg/agentic/systems/codex -run '^TestKnownCodexPolicyConflictMatrix$'` | 1 | Killed; long alias rows admitted |
+| Codex `-s` / `--sandbox` aliases | `go test ./pkg/agentic/systems/codex -run '^TestKnownCodexPolicyConflictMatrix$'` | 1 | Killed; long alias rows admitted |
+| Codex `--approve-for-me` | `go test ./pkg/agentic/systems/codex -run '^TestKnownCodexPolicyConflictMatrix$'` | 1 | Killed; yolo rows admitted |
+| Codex dangerous-bypass wildcard | `go test ./pkg/agentic/systems/codex -run '^TestKnownCodexPolicyConflictMatrix$'` | 1 | Killed; the synthetic future-prefix row was admitted |
+| Codex policy config keys | `go test ./pkg/agentic/systems/codex -run '^TestKnownCodexPolicyConflictMatrix$'` | 1 | Killed; `sandbox_permissions` rows admitted |
+| Codex mapped-bypass duplicate classification | `go test ./pkg/agentic/systems/codex -run '^TestKnownCodexPolicyConflictMatrix$'` | 1 | Killed; equals form lost the duplicate sentinel (still refused by wildcard fallback) |
+
+## Validation
+
+Commands rerun during this handoff:
+
+| Command | Exit | Result |
+|---|---:|---|
+| `go test ./pkg/agentic ./pkg/agentic/systems/claude ./pkg/agentic/systems/codex` | 0 | Focused packages passed |
+| `go test ./...` | 0 | All packages passed |
+| `go vet ./...` | 0 | Passed |
+| `go build ./...` | 0 | Passed |
+| `golangci-lint run --new` | 0 | 0 new issues |
+| `gofmt -l` on all eight changed Go files | 0 | No files reported |
+| `git diff --check` | 0 | Passed |
+| Ten targeted narrowing-mutant commands above | 1 each | Expected failing exits; all mutants killed |
+
+The previously attached run evidence reports `golangci-lint run` exit 1 for 20 existing findings in unchanged files. I did not rerun the full repository lint; I reran `golangci-lint run --new` and it reported no findings. No real provider CLI was invoked. No `LOGBOOK.md` was written, as the task brief explicitly forbids it.
